{"nodes": [{"id": "packages_docs_docs_architecture_overview_layered_architecture", "label": "dcmjs Layered Architecture (layers 0-2 + adapters)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/docs/docs/architecture/overview.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each layer only knows the layers below: layer 0 the dependency-free offset tokenizer, layer 1 the data model (lazy core, VR classes, writer, dictionary), layer 2 features (anonymizer, SR, derivations), adapters outside the stack consuming the public API. Arrows only point downward; the parser never imports dcmjs, the dictionary, or character sets by design."}, {"id": "packages_docs_docs_architecture_overview_derivability_argument", "label": "The Derivability Argument (offsets over eager values)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/docs/docs/architecture/overview.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Offsets can always produce values (decode lazily, with any charset, or never) but eager values can never recover offsets \u2014 once decoded, the exact header framing, padding, and delimiters are gone. Recording offsets is therefore the more fundamental representation, enabling both lazy reads and byte-faithful writes; startOffset/endOffset were added because dataOffset alone is ambiguous (header size depends on VR; corrected lengths exclude delimiters)."}], "edges": [{"source": "packages_docs_docs_architecture_overview_layered_architecture", "target": "packages_docs_docs_architecture_parser_package_dcmjs_parser", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "packages/docs/docs/architecture/overview.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "packages_docs_docs_architecture_overview_layered_architecture", "target": "packages_docs_docs_architecture_lazy_core_lazy_read_co